{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01169",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 6.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.45,
      "end_seconds": 11.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.63,
      "end_seconds": 20.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.16,
      "end_seconds": 24.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.6,
      "end_seconds": 29.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "It's a swollen painful calf, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.05,
      "end_seconds": 33.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.28,
      "end_seconds": 38.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Febuxostat, 80 milligrams, maybe, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.48,
      "end_seconds": 43.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.21,
      "end_seconds": 58.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.34,
      "text": "not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week. Before this I was on aspirin; that's been stopped"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.89,
      "end_seconds": 66.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.37,
      "end_seconds": 69.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "It's been five days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.76,
      "end_seconds": 75.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.4,
      "end_seconds": 83.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.58,
      "end_seconds": 94.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.79,
      "end_seconds": 96.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I'd call it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.1,
      "end_seconds": 102.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.71,
      "end_seconds": 109.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "it happens a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.57,
      "end_seconds": 114.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "okay, have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.19,
      "end_seconds": 131.79,
      "duration_seconds": 16.6,
      "text": "when it starts I tend to get sharp pain when I breathe in as well. The sharp pain when I breathe in? That's been for about a month. I've been coughing up a little blood too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.42,
      "end_seconds": 144.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "did you get fever, chest tightness or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.13,
      "end_seconds": 157.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "no, no fever, no chest tightness, no wheeze i did have sudden shortness of breath at one point, but that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.63,
      "end_seconds": 161.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.36,
      "end_seconds": 165.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.63,
      "end_seconds": 169.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.03,
      "end_seconds": 173.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.59,
      "end_seconds": 183.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.31,
      "end_seconds": 188.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.23,
      "end_seconds": 193.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.98,
      "end_seconds": 198.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Yes, gout. Heart disease, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.94,
      "end_seconds": 201.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.88,
      "end_seconds": 212.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "I've had thin bones for two years now. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.17,
      "end_seconds": 225.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "right, so gout and thin bones are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.23,
      "end_seconds": 239.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I quit smoking around ten years ago. I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 241.22,
      "end_seconds": 251.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 24, oxygen saturation is 94 percent, pulse is 104 beats a minute, BP is 136 over 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.74,
      "end_seconds": 254.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.14,
      "end_seconds": 259.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.72,
      "end_seconds": 278.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.67,
      "end_seconds": 282.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.0,
      "end_seconds": 301.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Your left calf is swollen and tender, and your oxygen is lower than I'd like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.38,
      "end_seconds": 318.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.96,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably a possible blood clot in the lung. It could also be a chest infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.11,
      "end_seconds": 325.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.68,
      "end_seconds": 346.05,
      "duration_seconds": 18.37,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a possible blood clot in the lung, but I'd like to confirm. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a swollen painful calf for five days, severe, and no wheeze or chest tightness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.64,
      "end_seconds": 350.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.62,
      "end_seconds": 355.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "let's get a CT scan of the chest, for breathlessness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.83,
      "end_seconds": 359.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.25,
      "end_seconds": 386.29,
      "duration_seconds": 25.04,
      "text": "I want a D-dimer blood test done, that's for possible clot. You need to go to hospital now for a scan. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. If you feel faint, that's the point to come in urgently. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.85,
      "end_seconds": 391.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "thank you, um, that's helpful"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.89,
      "end_seconds": 393.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Right, take care now."
    }
  ]
}